@startuml StateMachine_Award_Request
!theme plain
skinparam state {
    BackgroundColor<<draft>> LightBlue
    BackgroundColor<<pending>> LightYellow
    BackgroundColor<<review>> Orange
    BackgroundColor<<escalated>> LightCoral
    BackgroundColor<<approved>> LightGreen
    BackgroundColor<<rejected>> Pink
    BackgroundColor<<returned>> LightGray
    BackgroundColor<<archived>> DarkGray
}

title Award Request State Machine Diagram

note as AsBuilt
    <b>Transition table of ADR-023 (Feature 4.1 §7.2)</b>
    States are request statuses (<i>award_requests.status</i>);
    the award status (<i>awards.status</i>) follows in brackets.
    "Level" is <i>current_level</i>: FACULTY_SECRETARY, DEAN,
    RECTOR_SECRETARY, RECTOR. A level whose only reviewer
    would be the submitter is passed over (AC-0.6).
    Decisions are taken in SUBMITTED, ESCALATED or IN_REVIEW;
    an unclaimed request is claimed by the decision itself.
    EXPIRED stays in the check constraint, unused.
    Overdue: mark only. The hourly job sets overdue_noticed_at
    once per level and e-mails the next level; status, level
    and reviewer stay; every new deadline clears the mark (4.2.2).
end note

[*] --> DRAFT <<draft>> : Owner creates award

state DRAFT <<draft>> : award DRAFT; edited, documents\nattached or deleted by its owner only

DRAFT --> SUBMITTED <<pending>> : submit\n/ start level (AC-0.6), deadline,\naward PENDING

state SUBMITTED <<pending>> : awaiting a reviewer at the level
state ESCALATED <<escalated>> : awaiting a reviewer at a higher level\nafter a decision below
state IN_REVIEW <<review>> : claimed by one reviewer\n(current_reviewer_id)

SUBMITTED --> IN_REVIEW : claim
ESCALATED --> IN_REVIEW : claim
IN_REVIEW --> SUBMITTED : release\n[no decision below]
IN_REVIEW --> ESCALATED : release\n[a lower level decided]
IN_REVIEW --> IN_REVIEW : hand-over, take-over

state "SUBMITTED, ESCALATED, IN_REVIEW" as Open <<review>>
Open --> APPROVED <<approved>> : approve\n[level >= category minimum]\n/ award APPROVED
Open --> ESCALATED : approve [level < category minimum]\nescalate [level < RECTOR]\n/ next level not passed over,\nnew deadline, reviewer cleared
Open --> RETURNED <<returned>> : return [comment]\n/ award DRAFT, reviewer and\ndeadline cleared
Open --> REJECTED <<rejected>> : reject [comment]\n/ rejection_reason, award REJECTED

SUBMITTED --> WITHDRAWN : withdraw [no reviewer]\n/ award DRAFT (4.1.3)
ESCALATED --> WITHDRAWN : withdraw [no reviewer]\n/ award DRAFT (4.1.3)

state RETURNED <<returned>> : award DRAFT; owner corrects
state WITHDRAWN <<draft>> : award DRAFT; owner took it back

RETURNED --> SUBMITTED : resubmit\n/ same level (or next not passed over),\naward PENDING (4.1.3)
WITHDRAWN --> SUBMITTED : resubmit\n/ start level, award PENDING (4.1.3)

state APPROVED <<approved>> : final; verification badge when\nthe reviewer checked the documents
state REJECTED <<rejected>> : final; reason shown to the owner

APPROVED --> ARCHIVED <<archived>> : retention period elapsed (award status)
REJECTED --> [*]
ARCHIVED --> [*]

legend right
    |= State |= Award |= Description |
    | SUBMITTED | PENDING | Awaiting a reviewer at the start level |
    | IN_REVIEW | PENDING | Claimed by one reviewer |
    | ESCALATED | PENDING | Awaiting a reviewer at a higher level |
    | RETURNED | DRAFT | Sent back for corrections |
    | WITHDRAWN | DRAFT | Taken back by the owner before a claim |
    | APPROVED | APPROVED | Final |
    | REJECTED | REJECTED | Final |
endlegend

@enduml
